### Data Cleaning

#### Renaming columns

```{r}
#rename the columns
mwq_data_2020_current<-
  mwq_data_2020_current |> 
  dplyr::rename( Sampling_location = "Refer to map for pond #s, marsh units", 
          Date = "mm/dd/yyyy",
          Time = "24hr",
          Collection_method = "How was sample taken? Wading, kayak, etc.",
          Recorder = "Who sampled?", 
          Dawn_Dusk = "Y/N",
          Weather = "Temp, conditions",
          Tide = "High/Med/Low",
          Staff_Gauge_ft = "ft, gradations in 10ths",
          Depth_ft =  "ft, gradations of inches",
          pH = "...11", 
          Surface_temp = "degrees C...12",
          EC_surface = "mS...13",
          TDS_surface = "ppt...14",
          Salinity_surface = "ppt...15",
          DO_surface = "mg/L...16",
          DO_temp = "degrees C...17",
          Temp_deep = "degrees C...18",
          EC_deep = "mS...19",
          TDS_deep = "ppt...20",
          Salinity_deep = "ppt...21",
          pH_deep = "...22",
          DO_deep = "mg/L...23",
          Notes = "anything that might affect water quality-inverts, algae, temp, weather, etc"
          )
#fixing the time column since importing the file added a random date into the time column, making it time only
mwq_data_2020_current$Time <- format(mwq_data_2020_current$Time, format = "%H:%M:%S")

view(mwq_data_2020_current)
```

#### Mutating columns

```{r}
glimpse(mwq_data_2020_current)
#mutating columns to be properly read as numeric or characters
#need staff gauge,depth, surface temp, ec, tds, salinity,DO temp to be numeric
mwq_data_2020_current |> 
  mutate(Staff_Gauge_ft = as.numeric(Staff_Gauge_ft),
         Depth_ft = as.numeric(Depth_ft),
         Surface_temp = as.numeric(Surface_temp),
         EC_surface = as.numeric(EC_surface),
         TDS_surface = as.numeric(TDS_surface),
         Salinity_surface = as.numeric(Salinity_surface),
         DO_temp = as.numeric(DO_temp))



```

#### Selecting only relevant data

```{r}

#selecting only relevant columns, don't need any deep data since they only collected this data for a short period of time and then stopped taking it, they believed that the ponds at the SJM are not actually deep enough to have a significant difference in these measurements at the bottom of the ponds compared to the middle of the water column, drop pH since unreliable
mwq_cleandata<-
  mwq_data_2020_current |> 
  select(Sampling_location, Date, Time, Collection_method, Dawn_Dusk, Weather, Tide, Staff_Gauge_ft, Depth_ft, Surface_temp, EC_surface, TDS_surface, Salinity_surface, Salinity_surface, Notes)

#separate data by dawn dusk samples vs non dawn dusk samples, Julie said that the dawn dusk samples would show differences with non samples because temps would be lower since the samples were taken earlier in the day vs non samples that were mostly samples in the afternoon, Julie also wants to see if time/seasonality are factors

#dis da dawn dusk data
mwq_dd_data <-
  mwq_cleandata |> 
  filter(Dawn_Dusk == "Y")

#dis da non dawn dusk data, wrote it this way because i thought there were NAs in this column but apparently not lol

mwq_nondd_data<-
  mwq_cleandata |> 
  filter( ! Dawn_Dusk == "Y")

#i think that depth and staff gauge needs to be changed so unit matches up, will worry about that later, depth may be a nothing burger 
```

